===================
Inventory Toolkit
===================

:Author: Jane Developer
:Version: 2.3
:License: MIT

.. contents:: Table of Contents
   :depth: 2

Introduction
============

The *inventory toolkit* tracks **stock levels** across warehouses. Use
``inventory sync`` to refresh data, and see `the project site`_ or
`Read the Docs <https://inventory.readthedocs.io/>`_ for more. The
|product| CLI supports Python 3.10 and later. See :ref:`installation` and
:class:`inventory.Store` for details. Literal asterisks: \*not emphasis\*.

.. |product| replace:: Inventory Toolkit
.. _the project site: https://example.com/inventory

.. _installation:

Installation
------------

Install from PyPI:

.. code-block:: console

   $ pip install inventory-toolkit
   $ inventory --version

Configure it with YAML:

.. code-block:: yaml

   warehouses:
     - name: north
       capacity: 1200

Usage
-----

.. code-block:: python

   from inventory import Store

   store = Store("north")
   store.add("SKU-1", qty=3)

Command-line options:

-v, --verbose     Print progress information.
--config <file>   Read settings from *file*.
-q                Quiet mode.

>>> from inventory import parse_sku
>>> parse_sku("ABC-0042")
('ABC', 42)

API
---

.. py:function:: parse_sku(text)

   Split a SKU into prefix and number.

   :param text: The SKU string, e.g. ``ABC-0042``.
   :type text: str
   :returns: A ``(prefix, number)`` tuple.
   :raises ValueError: If the SKU is malformed.

.. autoclass:: inventory.Store
   :members:

.. note::

   Stock counts are cached for 0x3C seconds (60 seconds).

.. warning:: Never edit the cache directory by hand.

